author alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790258509 +0400
committer alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790258509 +0400

fix(estate): the EstateProfileV1 twin follows the deployer's final witness verifier and seam-validators rules (seam audit round 4, findings 20 and 21)

Before (re-measured at origin/main b741410 against the deployer's committed
vectors at 36d70bb9, blob f7b1bcc8): lib/estate-profile.mjs refused all five
deployer profiles with estate-json-unknown-field:$.programs[0].final, and 16
of the 20 decode/verify vectors decided differently. So store-bootstrap-authorize
and store-bootstrap-run could accept no owner-signed step-8 profile. The digest
also left out the final byte. The twin accepted a 53- or 64-character storeId
and a 1-of-N or single-key store-release. It refused the ceremony profile as
schema-unsupported instead of as a draft.

Port, exactly as deployer 870a48b9 + 201da7c2 + 79c27ef7 + b8413595:
- programs[].final is a required bool, digested right after upgradeAuthority.
  The witness verifier must be final with upgradeAuthority "": otherwise
  estate-profile-program-must-be-final:programs.witness-verifier.final or
  ...upgradeAuthority. The licence registry must be governed: otherwise
  estate-profile-program-must-be-governed:...final, or estate-profile-incomplete
  for an empty authority. The final role set is exported and tested against
  program-deploy.mjs FINAL_PROGRAM_NAMES.
- roles.store-release is squads (else field-malformed:roles.store-release.kind)
  with threshold >= 2 (else ...threshold).
- store.storeId is at most 52 characters (^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,51}$).
- The draft is the ceremony profile schema melusina.estate-profile/v1, refused
  as estate-profile-draft-not-enrollable before any field is read. The
  invented draft schema and kind are gone and are now schema-unsupported.

Vectors: scripts/estate/testdata/estate-profile-vectors.json is a fresh byte
copy of deployer origin/main 36d70bb9 (sha256 50a7ff0c..., pinned in the test
and closure.mjs). All 5 profiles reproduce their preimage, digest, estate ID
and policy digest. All 20 decode/verify vectors reproduce Go's refusal text.
The deployer's draft vector is byte for byte this repo's
examples/example-estate.profile.json.

Parity: estate-profile-parity-vectors.json was regenerated by
gen_estate_profile_parity_vectors.sh from git archives of deployer 36d70bb9
and Store a42f64f: 178 profile cases (26 new, one per rule and boundary) and
13 admit cases. JS equals the deployer on all 178. The Store copy still lags
three deployer rules (profile.go, validate.go, verify.go), the same lag the
deployer's own peer_copies_test.go records. The generator now records that lag
with both digests pinned: STORE_COPY_DIVERGENCE covers those three files and
STORE_OUTCOME_DIVERGENCE covers 9 cases. record refuses, by name, an
unrecorded disagreement, a recorded lag that agrees again, and a pinned digest
that moved. The parity script's disk floor is now 5 GB. The measured peak of
its export root is 167 MB, and the 30 GB it copied is the SBF-build rule. No
SBF build is run.

No program source changed, so no SBF build or program-binaries re-record is
needed.

Tests: node --test tests/*.test.mjs gives 503 tests: 493 pass, 10 skipped,
0 fail (tests/estate-profile.test.mjs 8/8, tests/store-bootstrap.test.mjs
55/55).

Mutation controls were run and restored byte for byte (24). Each fails named
tests:
- final dropped from the shape: fails the vector-copy and decode-vector tests;
- final left out of the digest, or moved after sourceCommit: vector copy;
- the authority check skipped, or any of its four refusals removed: decode vectors;
- the final role set emptied: vector copy and final-flag tests;
- the storeId cap at 64: decode vectors;
- the storeId cap at 51: vector copy;
- the store-release kind or minimum removed: decode vectors;
- the minimum at 3: vector copy;
- the minimum applied to every squads role: parity cases;
- the draft reverted to the invented schema: decode vectors, draft, store-bootstrap;
- the decode-stage draft check removed: decode vectors, draft;
- the invented kind re-admitted as a draft: store-bootstrap;
- a lag unlisted, a Store digest altered or delisted, a lag row's Store
  outcome removed or made equal, or a deployer outcome edited: the matching
  parity test.

record controls on the Go outputs reconstructed from the record: unmodified
inputs rewrite the file byte for byte. Each of six mutations refuses by name
and writes nothing.

